// Planted for app/test_suppose.mjs (17 Oct 2026): two convergent arguments for one conclusion, an
// objection with a reply, an undercut, an attack on a whole argument, a contradictory pair, a step
// named deductive, and a formalized modus ponens, valid and invalid.
===
title: "Planted -- suppositions and contraposition"
===

[Main]: The main conclusion holds.

<Linked>: Two premises together.

(1) [P1]: The first premise holds.
(2) [P2]: The second premise holds.
----
(3) [Main]

<Alone>: A reason on its own.

(1) [P3]: The third premise holds.
----
(2) [Main]

[Obj]: Something tells against the first premise.
    -> [P1]

[Reply]: The objection misreads the first premise.
    -> [Obj]

[Under]: The third premise does not bear on the conclusion.
    _> <Alone>

[Whole]: The linked argument fails somewhere.
    -> <Linked>

[Rival]: The third premise is false.
    >< [P3]

[Named]: A conclusion reached by a named rule.

<Ponens>: Named, not formalized.

(1) [If A then B]: If a then b.
(2) [A]: A holds.
-- Modus ponens --
(3) [Named]

[Formal]: B holds, formally.
    {formalization: "b"}

<Checked>: A formalized modus ponens.

(1) [Rule]: If a then b, formally.
    {formalization: "a -> b"}
(2) [Fact]: A holds, formally.
    {formalization: "a"}
-- Modus ponens --
(3) [Formal]

[Wrong]: A holds, by affirming the consequent.
    {formalization: "a"}

<Affirming>: An invalid step.

(1) [Rule]
(2) [Formal]
-- Modus ponens --
(3) [Wrong]
